From: Gigi <42325924+g-cqd@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:54:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Web Extensions: ws and wss match patterns parse, as in
 Firefox and Chrome (Sunset W7)

webRequest.onBeforeRequest.addListener(listener, { urls: [..., 'ws://*/*', 'wss://*/*'] }) was refused whole: 'ws' was
not a valid scheme. Firefox and Chrome accept WebSocket patterns in filters; uBlock Origin listens on them at its start.

ws and wss join the valid schemes only: the supported ones (what a host permission can grant) are unchanged.

diff --git a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Extensions/WebExtensionMatchPattern.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Extensions/WebExtensionMatchPattern.cpp
index c4251a87a..7e8277e74 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Extensions/WebExtensionMatchPattern.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Extensions/WebExtensionMatchPattern.cpp
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@ WebExtensionMatchPattern::URLSchemeSet& WebExtensionMatchPattern::extensionSchem
 
 WebExtensionMatchPattern::URLSchemeSet& WebExtensionMatchPattern::validSchemes()
 {
-    static MainRunLoopNeverDestroyed<URLSchemeSet> schemes = std::initializer_list<String> { "*"_s, "http"_s, "https"_s, "file"_s, "ftp"_s, "webkit-extension"_s };
+    static MainRunLoopNeverDestroyed<URLSchemeSet> schemes = std::initializer_list<String> { "*"_s, "http"_s, "https"_s, "ws"_s, "wss"_s, "file"_s, "ftp"_s, "webkit-extension"_s };
     return schemes;
 }
 
